  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 22,
    "summary": "A good name is better than riches—Train up a child in the way he should go.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "A good name is rather to be chosen than great riches, and loving favour rather than silver and gold.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "Eccl. 7:1; 1 Ne. 1:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 6
          },
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The rich and poor meet together: the Lord is the maker of them all.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Mosiah 4:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A prudent man foreseeth the evil, and hideth himself: but the simple pass on, and are punished.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Prudence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "By humility and the fear of the Lord are riches, and honour, and life.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "TG Humility."
          },
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "OR reverence of the Lord. 2 Ne. 1:20; Mosiah 2:24 (21–25). TG Reverence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thorns and snares are in the way of the froward: he that doth keep his soul shall be far from them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "OR perverse."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "Eph. 6:4 (1–4). TG Education; Family, Children, Responsibilities toward; Marriage, Fatherhood; Teaching."
          },
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Children."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The rich ruleth over the poor, and the borrower is servant to the lender.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "D&C 19:35."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "TG Borrow; Debt."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Servant."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that soweth iniquity shall reap vanity: and the rod of his anger shall fail.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Harvest."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that hath a bountiful eye shall be blessed; for he giveth of his bread to the poor.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Bread."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "TG Almsgiving."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Cast out the scorner, and contention shall go out; yea, strife and reproach shall cease.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Contention."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that loveth pureness of heart, for the grace of his lips the king shall be his friend.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The eyes of the Lord preserve knowledge, and he overthroweth the words of the transgressor.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The slothful man saith, There is a lion without, I shall be slain in the streets.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The mouth of strange women is a deep pit: he that is abhorred of the Lord shall fall therein.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Fornication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Foolishness is bound in the heart of a child; but the rod of correction shall drive it far from him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that oppresseth the poor to increase his riches, and he that giveth to the rich, shall surely come to want.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Oppression."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 50
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 89
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 101
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Bow down thine ear, and hear the words of the wise, and apply thine heart unto my knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For it is a pleasant thing if thou keep them within thee; they shall withal be fitted in thy lips.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "That thy trust may be in the Lord, I have made known to thee this day, even to thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Have not I written to thee excellent things in counsels and knowledge,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "That I might make thee know the certainty of the words of truth; that thou mightest answer the words of truth to them that send unto thee?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "D&C 18:3; 98:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Rob not the poor, because he is poor: neither oppress the afflicted in the gate:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Zech. 7:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the Lord will plead their cause, and spoil the soul of those that spoiled them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "Ps. 35:10; Prov. 23:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "D&C 124:75."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Make no friendship with an angry man; and with a furious man thou shalt not go:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Friendship."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Lest thou learn his ways, and get a snare to thy soul.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be not thou one of them that strike hands, or of them that are sureties for debts.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "IE shake hands, showing agreement."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "Prov. 6:1; 11:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou hast nothing to pay, why should he take away thy bed from under thee?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Remove not the ancient landmark, which thy fathers have set.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Deut. 19:14; Job 24:2; Prov. 23:10; Hosea 5:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Seest thou a man diligent in his business? he shall stand before kings; he shall not stand before mean men.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Diligence."
          },
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "OR obscure, or wicked (men)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 106
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 107
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
